AUDIO: 'description, and there you\'ll find our videos and analysis and articles about everything going on in the EV world. Here\'s the part most coverage skips, though. This plant is being finished at'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the exact moment the rest of the green green hydrogen industry is falling apart. Uh it\'s not going well. Analysts ING counted roughly 50 publicly canceled hydrogen projects'

[02:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in what\'s been called the industry\'s year of reckoning, because green hydrogen still costs around $4.50 to $6 per kilogram in favorable regions versus $1.50 to'

[03:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '$2.50 for fossil-based gray hydrogen. In other words, green hydrogen is on average about two to three times more expensive'

[03:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'than fossil fuel-based hydrogen. Gigawatt-scale export projects in Canada stalled this year for one simple reason: no buyers. NEOM survived because it solved that'

[03:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'problem before pouring concrete. Air Products signed an exclusive 30-year off-take agreement for every ton of ammonia the plant produces, which unlocked $6.1 billion in US'

[03:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'dollars in financing from 23 banks. Every kilogram already has a customer for the next three decades. Air Products is also finalizing a deal with Norway\'s Yara'

[04:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to market that ammonia globally through its shipping fleet. And the competition is it\'s real, actually. Envision Energy in China commissioned its own giant off-grid hydrogen to ammonia plant last year. Starting at 300,000 tons annually and'

[04:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scaling toward 1.5 million tons with a landmark off-take deal signed with Japan\'s Marubeni. Saudi Arabia\'s answer to all this? Go bigger. A lot bigger.'

[04:30] [scene:talk]
